# IBM Cloud and IBM Granite Integration

## IBM Services Used

This project uses IBM Granite through IBM watsonx.ai as the primary AI model.

IBM Cloud Code Engine is used for application deployment.

## IBM Granite

IBM Granite is responsible for:

- Understanding user travel requirements
- Generating personalized itineraries
- Providing travel recommendations
- Generating travel tips
- Answering travel-related questions
- Modifying existing itineraries

## IBM watsonx.ai

The backend connects to IBM watsonx.ai using the IBM Cloud API credentials and project ID.

The Granite model is configured using:

GRANITE_MODEL_ID

## IBM Cloud Code Engine

The FastAPI backend can be deployed using IBM Cloud Code Engine.

## Security

API keys and credentials are stored in environment variables.

No credentials are committed to GitHub.

## Demo Mode

The application supports DEMO_MODE for demonstrations when IBM Cloud credentials are unavailable.
